; The inverse trig family and the two angle-unit conversions. `sin`/`cos`/
; `tan` were pinned when `src/trig.zig` was vendored to make them
; host-independent; their inverses were added to the same table and never
; got a fixture, so nothing held their digits between the native build and
; the two WASM artifacts.
;
; Form 1 is the one to watch: (acos 0.5) is 1.0471975511965979, and pi/3
; correctly rounded is 1.0471975511965976. The implementation is three ulp
; off the true value — which is fine and normal for a software inverse
; cosine, and is exactly why the digits have to be written down rather than
; recomputed by whoever reads this next.
;
; Forms 3/4/5 walk `atan2` out of the first quadrant, where the sign
; handling lives: same |y| and |x|, three different answers, and (atan2 0
; -1) lands exactly on +pi rather than -pi.
(asin 0.5)
(acos 0.5)
(atan 1.0)
(atan2 1.0 1.0)
(atan2 1.0 -1.0)
(atan2 0.0 -1.0)
(radians 180.0)
(degrees 3.141592653589793)
(pi)
(tau)
